Now let's design the fix. Add a helper to check whether a site's tensor is zero. For COLLINEAR, `is_zero(cell->tensors[i], mag_symprec)`; for NONCOLLINEAR, `is_zero_d3(&cell->tensors[3*i], mag_symprec)` but note is_zero_d3 expects `const double a[3]`. `&cell->tensors[3*i]` works if tensors is flat array. But `is_zero_d3` is local static, defined later in file (line ~820). We can use it.

In the j loop, for COLLINEAR:
```c
if (cell->tensor_rank == COLLINEAR &&
    !(is_zero(cell->tensors[i], mag_symprec) &&
      is_zero(cell->tensors[j], mag_symprec)) &&
    !is_zero(cell->tensors[j] - scalar, mag_symprec)) {
    continue;
}
```
Wait, condition should be: if both source i and candidate j are zero, skip the tensor diff check (i.e., don't `continue`). Otherwise, require diff < mag_symprec. So:
```c
if (cell->tensor_rank == COLLINEAR &&
    !(is_zero(cell->tensors[i], mag_symprec) &&
      is_zero(cell->tensors[j], mag_symprec)) &&
    !is_zero(cell->tensors[j] - scalar, mag_symprec)) {
    continue;
}
```
This is logically: if NOT (both zero) AND diff not zero -> continue (reject). Equivalent to: if both zero -> don't reject based on tensor; else reject if diff not zero.

